 {"kind": "fits", "text": "ok so our claims-triage agent (ADK, running on Cloud Run, Gemini 2.5 Flash) finished its 6-week pilot with the ops team. I've got the eval results in evals/pilot_summary.csv, the BigQuery cost export, and a doc of feedback from the adjusters. VP of Operations decides next Thursday whether we go to prod for all three regions. Can you help me put together a deck outline where every claim points back to an actual number from those files, talking points for me, the questions she's likely to grill me on (she always asks about error rates on edge cases and who's on the hook when it's wrong), and a one-page memo she can read beforehand?"},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "Agent's been live for 3 months now. Sponsor wants a monthly update on value vs spend — tickets deflected, hours saved, GCP bill, that kind of thing. We have the Vertex AI usage logs and the Zendesk export. Need a template for this report plus a draft of the October one. Keep it short, he doesn't read past page one."},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "Our ADK agent's costs are way higher than what I put in the pilot proposal and finance is asking questions. Looking at the traces, it seems like the planner sub-agent is calling the search tool 4-5 times per request and re-sending the full conversation history each time. Can you look at agents/planner.py and figure out how to cut down the token usage without tanking answer quality?", "needs_instead": "Technical cost optimization: debugging the agent's tool-calling loop and context handling in code to reduce token spend, not preparing a decision deck or stakeholder report."}
